The following parts of this package are ports or adaptations of Agentless
code, rewritten for this package's value objects and error handling but
keeping the upstream semantics:

  * crates/facts/src/slices.rs
        line wrapping and interval merging, from Agentless
        agentless/util/preprocess_data.py

  * crates/facts/src/locs.rs
        the location grammar and its transfer onto extracted symbols, from
        Agentless agentless/util/preprocess_data.py
        (transfer_arb_locs_to_locs)

  * crates/patch/src/blocks.rs
        the SEARCH/REPLACE edit format and its parser, from Agentless
        agentless/util/postprocess_data.py

  * crates/patch/src/vote.rs
        the candidate filter ladder and the majority-vote ranking key, from
        Agentless agentless/repair/rerank.py

The wheel and the sdist ship this file in a notices/ directory, together
with the licenses of the third-party code that the binaries hold. In the
repository, packaging/notices.sh writes that directory. Its paths are:

  * THIRD-PARTY-CRATES.md
        the Rust crates that the binaries link, with each license text

  * grammars/MANIFEST.toml and grammars/licenses/
        the pinned tree-sitter grammars and tree-sitter-language-pack, with
        the license of each

  * grammars/shim/utf8proc/LICENSE.md
        the license of utf8proc, which the binaries link for the grammar
        scanners' character classes

